WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.718 --> 00:00:06.439
From Gucci to Chanel, Topshop to Primark,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.747
clothes industry heavyweights
rely on fashion forecasters

00:00:09.747 --> 00:00:12.119
for next season's new look.

00:00:12.119 --> 00:00:14.185
But advancements in
artificial intelligence

00:00:14.185 --> 00:00:17.828
are about to turn their
art into a science.

00:00:17.828 --> 00:00:21.141
Cognitive Computing is now
able to identify patterns

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:24.009
previously inaccessible to humans.

00:00:24.009 --> 00:00:28.098
It can simultaneously analyze
vast amounts of global data,

00:00:28.098 --> 00:00:31.033
from social media buzz to political polls,

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:33.909
making it possible to accurately spot

00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:36.076
what's hot and what's not.

00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:41.743
WGSN, the world's biggest
fashion forecaster,

00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:45.731
now uses AI alongside
more traditional methods,

00:00:45.731 --> 00:00:50.731
a move that could reduce
forecasting errors by up to 50%.

00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:55.916
Trendspotting mistakes can
have far-reaching consequences.

00:00:55.916 --> 00:00:59.326
H&amp;M recently confessed to a $4.3 billion

00:00:59.326 --> 00:01:02.266
unsold stock mountain.

00:01:02.266 --> 00:01:07.038
Industry waste costs both
profits and reputation.

00:01:07.038 --> 00:01:11.044
Technology could make the fashion
industry more sustainable.

00:01:11.044 --> 00:01:14.178
By using machine
learning, an AI technique,

00:01:14.178 --> 00:01:16.175
to match supply with demand,

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:19.101
unnecessary manufacturing
could be limited,

00:01:19.101 --> 00:01:22.633
and fashion's environmental
footprint reduced.

00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:24.952
Online retailers are cottoning on.

00:01:24.952 --> 00:01:28.909
In the next two years,
75% of fashion retailers

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:31.076
plan to invest in AI.

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:35.216
But keeping up with tech
giants is going to be tough.

00:01:35.216 --> 00:01:38.127
Amazon is now developing what's
believed to be the world's

00:01:38.127 --> 00:01:40.745
first AI fashion designer.

00:01:40.745 --> 00:01:43.618
It plans to use an algorithm
that designs clothes

00:01:43.618 --> 00:01:47.473
by analyzing images and
copying popular styles,

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:50.938
using them to build
completely new designs.

00:01:50.938 --> 00:01:54.334
This technological makeover
could hold huge benefits,

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:57.695
especially for those
who like to shop online.

00:01:57.695 --> 00:02:00.441
A Japanese company has unveiled the ZOZO,

00:02:00.441 --> 00:02:03.245
a body measurement suit
that will ensure the clothes

00:02:03.245 --> 00:02:06.130
you order fit you perfectly,

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:09.149
all meaning our future
wardrobes could contain clothes

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:13.399
designed for us and sold
to us by technology alone.

